    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-delete for owners in this Spring Boot PetClinic REST app. The change spans the entity, persistence schema, the API contract, and the create/delete logic.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`), initialized to `false`, with getter/setter. So a newly created owner is `deleted = false`.\n\n2. **Database schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to the `owners` table. The default keeps existing seed rows non-deleted (their inserts use explicit column lists). Tests run on hsqldb; the app default is h2.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it. `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `deleted`.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`**:\n   - `deleteOwner` no longer hard-deletes. It sets `deleted = true` and saves, retaining the row and returning `204` (2xx). GET still returns the owner afterward with `deleted: true`.\n   - `findHouseholdMember` (the create endpoint's duplicate/identity check) now skips owners flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking household duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) pass.\n\nOne note: I kept the now-unused `ClinicService.deleteOwner` facade method (and the repository `delete` implementations) in place rather than removing them, since they're part of the shared repository contract across profiles and removing them is outside the scope of this change.",
